-- Row il-42. THE RATES OF APPRECIATION TAX ON AN INDIVIDUAL'S SALE OF A DWELLING: ss 48A(b), (b1), (b2), (c) and 48B.
-- The seller asks: "how much appreciation tax do I owe on this sale?"
-- ANSWER SHAPE. MAYBE NUMBER: shekels of tax, or NOTHING where the text stops short (listed below).
-- THE RATES ARE CONSOLIDATION-ONLY. The percentages of s 48A (25%, 20%, 10%, 0%) and the three days of s 47 were read from the Wikisource consolidation (revision 3085765, 2026-09-30) and NOT from the
-- instruments that amended s 48A. The amendments to s 48A listed by the consolidation were not read, so the commencement of the present wording is unknown to this encoding (fork F8 in NOTES.md).
-- ASSUMED, NOT READ: that the present wording of s 48A governs a sale on or after 1 June 2023, the day the same amending law (the 2023 amendment that also changed s 9) begins to count in s 9. A sale before
-- that day answers NOTHING.
-- THE ORDINANCE IS NOT ENCODED. Section 48A taxes real appreciation "at the rate of section 121 of the Ordinance, at up to 25%", and s 48B treats the appreciation as the top step of the seller's income.
-- The two rates the Ordinance fixes are therefore INPUTS the seller states (never a figure this encoding holds): see `The Ordinance rates you state`.
-- NOT ENCODED, with reasons (coverage table in NOTES.md): s 48A(b1)(3) and (b)(2) (the Director's power to allow a lower rate); s 48A(b3) and (b4) (rights to build more; a dwelling whose building is completed
-- after 31 December 2030); s 48A(d) (a right acquired before 1961); s 48A(e) (spreading the appreciation over up to four tax years, an election that only the seller makes and whose result depends on the seller's
-- other income in each year); s 48A1 (a temporary provision for sales to 31 December 2003, closed); s 48C (expropriation).

§ `Sections 48A, 48B: the tax on the appreciation`

DECLARE `The Ordinance rates you state` HAS
    `the rate at which section 121 of the Ordinance would tax the appreciation as the top step of your income` IS A NUMBER
    `the highest rate in section 121 of the Ordinance` IS A NUMBER

§§ `The rate caps`

-- s 48A(b)(1): an individual is liable to tax on real appreciation "in the rate of section 121 of the Ordinance, at up to 25%". s 48B(a): the appreciation is the top step of the seller's income and the rate does
-- not exceed 48A(b)(1).
-- src:621 | (ב)(1) יחיד יהיה חייב במס על שבח ריאלי כאמור בסעיף 121 לפקודה, בשיעור של עד 25%.
`the cap of section 48A(b)(1)` MEANS 0.25

-- s 48A(b1)(1)(b): the real appreciation after the start day and up to the change day: the rate of section 121, at up to 20%.
-- src:628 | (ב) על השבח הריאלי לאחר יום התחילה ועד למועד השינוי – בשיעור כאמור בסעיף 121 לפקודה עד 20%;
`the cap of section 48A(b1)(1)(b)` MEANS 0.2

-- s 48A(c)(1): the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount is 10%. s 48A(c)(2): 0% for a qualifying dwelling to which s 48A(b2) applies.
-- src:644 | (ג)(1) המס על הסכום האינפלציוני החייב יהיה 10% ושיעור זה יהיה גם השיעור לענין השומה על פי פקודת מס הכנסה.
-- src:645 | (2) על אף האמור בפסקה (1), במכירת דירת מגורים מזכה שחלות עליה הוראות סעיף קטן (ב2), ובכלל זה בנסיבות האמורות בסעיף קטן (ב3)(1), יהיה המס על הסכום האינפלציוני החייב בשיעור 0%, ושיעור זה יהיה גם השיעור לעניין השומה לפי פקודת מס הכנסה.
`the rate on the chargeable inflationary amount` MEANS 0.1

`the first day the present wording of section 48A is taken to govern` MEANS Date 1 6 2023

GIVEN r IS AN `The Ordinance rates you state`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate on the real appreciation after the change day` MEANS
    min (`the cap of section 48A(b)(1)`) (r's `the rate at which section 121 of the Ordinance would tax the appreciation as the top step of your income`)

GIVEN r IS AN `The Ordinance rates you state`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate on the real appreciation between the start day and the change day` MEANS
    min (`the cap of section 48A(b1)(1)(b)`) (r's `the rate at which section 121 of the Ordinance would tax the appreciation as the top step of your income`)

§§ `Which paragraph of section 48A reaches the sale`

-- s 48A(b2): on the sale of a qualifying dwelling acquired before the transition day, the real appreciation up to the transition day is exempt and the balance is taxed under (b)(1); the inflationary amount
-- is taxed at 0%.
-- src:632 | (ב2)(1) על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (ב)(1), במכירת דירת מגורים מזכה שיום רכישתה היה לפני יום המעבר, יחויב השבח הריאלי בהתאם להוראות אלה:
-- src:633 | (א) השבח הריאלי עד יום המעבר יהיה פטור ממס;
-- src:634 | (ב) על יתרת השבח הריאלי לאחר יום המעבר יחול מס בשיעור הקבוע בסעיף קטן (ב)(1).
-- src:635 | (2) הוראות סעיף קטן (ב)(2) יחולו, בשינויים המחויבים, על חיוב במס של יחיד לפי סעיף קטן זה.
GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 48A(b2) reaches the sale` MEANS
    `the dwelling is a qualifying dwelling` a AND a's `the day you acquired the right` LESS THAN (`the transition day`)

-- s 48A(b1): on the sale of any other right acquired before the change day, the real appreciation is charged in three parts (up to the start day, from the start day to the change day, the balance).
-- src:624 | (ב1) על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (ב)(1), במכירת זכות במקרקעין, למעט במכירת דירת מגורים מזכה שחלות לגבי מכירתה הוראות סעיפים קטנים (ב2) ו־(ב3), או בפעולה באיגוד מקרקעין שעשה יחיד, כשיום הרכישה של הזכות במקרקעין או באיגוד המקרקעין, לפי הענין, היה לפני מועד השינוי, יחולו הוראות אלה:
-- src:625 | (1) נרכש הנכס לפני יום התחילה, יחויב השבח הריאלי במס בשיעורים כמפורט להלן:
-- src:626 | (א) על השבח הריאלי עד יום התחילה – בשיעור המס הגבוה ביותר הקבוע בסעיף 121 לפקודה;
-- src:627 | [note: לעניין מכירת זכות מקרקעין, בידי יחיד, בתקופה שמיום כ׳ בטבת התשע״ו (1 בינואר 2016) עד יום כ״ג בטבת התשע״ט (31 בדצמבר 2018), ראו הוראת שעה בסעיף 10 לחוק ההתייעלות הכלכלית (תיקוני חקיקה להשגת יעדי התקציב לשנות התקציב 2015 ו־2016), התשע״ו–2015.]
-- src:628 | (ב) על השבח הריאלי לאחר יום התחילה ועד למועד השינוי – בשיעור כאמור בסעיף 121 לפקודה עד 20%;
-- src:629 | (ג) על יתרת השבח הריאלי לאחר מועד השינוי – בשיעור הקבוע בסעיף קטן (ב)(1) או (1א), לפי העניין;
GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 48A(b1) reaches the sale` MEANS
    (NOT (`section 48A(b2) reaches the sale` a)) AND (a's `the day you acquired the right` LESS THAN (`the change day`))

§§ `The tax on the real appreciation`

-- s 48A(b1)(1)(a): the real appreciation up to the start day is charged at "the highest tax rate fixed in section 121 of the Ordinance", with no cap.
-- src:626 | (א) על השבח הריאלי עד יום התחילה – בשיעור המס הגבוה ביותר הקבוע בסעיף 121 לפקודה;
GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`, r IS AN `The Ordinance rates you state`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the tax under section 48A(b2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parts of the real appreciation by the transition day` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST ((p's `after the transition day`) TIMES (`the rate on the real appreciation after the change day` r))

GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`, r IS AN `The Ordinance rates you state`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the tax under section 48A(b1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parts of the real appreciation` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        JUST (  (p's `up to the start day`) TIMES (r's `the highest rate in section 121 of the Ordinance`)
              PLUS (p's `after the start day up to the change day`) TIMES (`the rate on the real appreciation between the start day and the change day` r)
              PLUS (p's `after the change day`) TIMES (`the rate on the real appreciation after the change day` r))

GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`, r IS AN `The Ordinance rates you state`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the tax on the real appreciation, before any exemption` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a's `the day of the sale` LESS THAN (`the first day the present wording of section 48A is taken to govern`) THEN NOTHING
        IF a's `the day you acquired the right` AT MOST (Date 31 12 1960) THEN NOTHING
        IF `section 48A(b2) reaches the sale` a THEN `the tax under section 48A(b2)` a r
        IF `section 48A(b1) reaches the sale` a THEN `the tax under section 48A(b1)` a r
        OTHERWISE JUST ((`the real appreciation` a) TIMES (`the rate on the real appreciation after the change day` r))

§§ `The tax on the chargeable inflationary amount`

-- s 47 "chargeable inflationary amount": the inflationary amount that would have been chargeable had the right been sold on 31 December 1993 with the adjusted remaining acquisition value as the sale value.
-- READING TAKEN (fork F3 in NOTES.md): a right acquired on or after 1 January 1994 has no chargeable inflationary amount, since there is no 1993 sale of it to imagine, so the amount is 0. For a right acquired
-- before 1994 the amount needs the index on 31 December 1993 and a second adjusted value, which this encoding does not hold: NOTHING, except where the rate is 0%.
-- src:600 | ”סכום אינפלציוני חייב“ – הסכום האינפלציוני שהיה מתחייב במס אילו נמכרה זכות במקרקעין או נעשתה פעולה באיגוד מקרקעין, לפי הענין, ביום י״ז בטבת התשנ״ד (31 בדצמבר 1993) כששווי המכירה הוא יתרת שווי רכישה מתואמת;
GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 48A(b2) reaches the sale` a THEN JUST 0
        IF a's `the day you acquired the right` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 1994) THEN JUST 0
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `The tax on the sale`

-- The appreciation tax on the sale: the tax on the real appreciation plus the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount, for the part of the sale that stays taxable after the exemptions.
-- The seller states the two Ordinance rates; every other number is the Law's.
GIVEN a IS A `A sale of a dwelling`, r IS AN `The Ordinance rates you state`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the appreciation tax on your sale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fraction of the sale that stays taxable` a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fraction THEN
        CONSIDER `the tax on the real appreciation, before any exemption` a r
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST onReal THEN
            CONSIDER `the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount` a
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST onInflation THEN JUST (fraction TIMES (onReal PLUS onInflation))

-- Where the rates and the exemption figures behind the answer were read: the rates of s 48A from the consolidation alone, the exemption figures (when the exemption turns on one) from the official page.
GIVETH A `Where a figure was read`
`where the rates of section 48A were read` MEANS `the consolidation only`
